# Express API

## Layering (feature modules under `src/modules/<feature>/`)
- `*.routes.ts`: HTTP wiring only (path, middleware, controller method).
- `*.controller.ts`: parse/validate input, call service, shape response. No business logic, no DB access.
- `*.service.ts`: business rules. Framework-agnostic (no `req`/`res`).
- `*.repository.ts`: the only layer touching Mongoose models. Returns plain domain objects (`.lean()`), not documents.
- Cross-cutting code in `src/core/` (config, logger, errors, middleware, db, crypto).

## Dependency injection
- Constructor injection of interfaces. All wiring lives in `src/container.ts`. No `new` of collaborators inside classes, no module-level singletons imported by services.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
export class ZapService {
  constructor(private readonly zaps: ZapRepository, private readonly catalog: CatalogRegistry) {}
}
```

## Validation & errors
- Validate every body/query/param with Zod schemas from `@workflow/shared` via a `validate()` middleware.
- Throw `AppError` subclasses; one error middleware maps them to `{ error: { code, message } }`. Never leak stack traces or upstream payloads.
- Express 5: async handlers may throw; do not add try/catch just to call `next(err)`.

## Security
- Env read once through a Zod-validated `config`; fail fast at boot. Never read `process.env` elsewhere.
- Every Zap query is scoped by `ownerId` from the session. Never trust ids from the client for ownership.
- Webhooks: verify `X-Hub-Signature-256` with `crypto.timingSafeEqual` over the **raw** body; dedupe on `X-GitHub-Delivery`; respond fast (202).
- Tokens encrypted at rest; never logged. Use the structured logger (pino) with redaction, never `console`.
